  "curated": {
    "notes": [
      "Cordis layer model (DSH 0.2.0-rc.2): the effective config is composed from patch layers in bundle -> profile -> home -> --patch order, a later layer overriding entries with the same id. observed.projection.layers keeps each on-disk layer separate and in that order because the product selects a profile per invocation and persists no active profile, so no single composed view exists to publish; the desktop profile is the one DSH Desktop uses on this machine, and the home layer is present but empty ([]).",
      "Legacy settings.yaml is not a source any more: the product folds it into the Cordis entries once and renames it settings.yaml.imported (recorded with role imported-legacy-config and never parsed). Consequently the old settings.yaml-only semantics are gone - the agent-presets section and the .agent-presets preset list have no entries on this machine, so projection.agent_presets is absent instead of a fabricated mapping. reasoningEffort on agent-default-model is new in the Cordis shape and is projected.",
      "MCP entry ids in these layers (for example the web profile's mcp-parallel) are owned by context/configs/mcp.json, which reads the same patch layers; this profile records only the ids so nothing is silently lost. UI, permission and live-stats entry ids are deliberately unprojected: they are product behaviour, not machine facts. Only projection.layers[].entries subtrees are read, and headers/env values are never touched."
    ]
  },
